import sys; sys.path.insert(0,'..')
from con_helpers import *
save(3,7,"The Body and the Breath: Where the Energy Begins","Take hold of the slowest wave you have, the breath, and let the mind ride it down: four counts in, six counts out, for a few minutes a day. Notice what changes in your thoughts.",[
mc("U","What does Swamiji mean by ‘all force is prāṇa’, and what picture does he give?",
 ["One energy at different speeds and densities, like a keyboard from slow bass notes up to the finest.","Five separate energies in the body, each one running on its own and meeting the others at the heart.","A force that belongs only to the breath, which the mind and the body can borrow for a short time.","A name for the energy of the sun alone, which the living body takes in with its food and its air."],0,
 "Electricity in a wire, sunlight, the heartbeat, a thought and the deep peace of meditation are not five energies but one at different speeds. The body is the bass end, then breath, emotion, thought and subtlest awareness at the top. Slow the breath for a minute and your thoughts slow: one energy at two speeds.",
 "One energy, many speeds, one keyboard","Part 1"),
mc("A","James had half-thought that body work was a soft warm-up before the real mental discipline. How does Swamiji answer?",
 ["He agrees that it is a warm-up, since the body is the lower and slower end of the whole keyboard.","He says that it is the foundation: on one keyboard there is no lesser end, and you play from the bottom up.","He says it is not needed at all, since a trained mind can steady itself without the body’s help.","He says it is useful only to those who are ill, and a healthy person can skip straight to the mind."],1,
 "If the body were separate from the spirit, working with it would be a lower thing. But touching the body is touching the same living energy that becomes thought and awareness, only at its densest. You cannot steady the top of the keyboard while the bottom is crashing.",
 "The body is the foundation, not the preliminary","Part 1"),
mc("A","Sarah’s mind is still running at 3 a.m. a conversation that finished at dinner. Which of the five energies does Swamiji say is asking for help?",
 ["Prāṇa proper, the energy of taking in, which is flooded and so cannot stop receiving.","Apāna, the energy of letting go, which has gone weak, so nothing in her can put the thing down.","Udāna, the upward energy of expression, which has gone slack, so that she cannot speak up.","Vyāna, the pervading energy, which is blocked, so that the parts of her do not talk to one another."],1,
 "Apāna is the out-breath, elimination, and in the mind the releasing of finished thoughts. The handle is the long exhale, the body’s own gesture of putting down. Not arguing with the thoughts, but lengthening the out-breath for a few minutes.",
 "Weak letting-go keeps a finished thing ringing","Part 2"),
mc("A","A pupil takes in a hard lesson but never seems to absorb it. Which energy does this suggest, and what is the remedy?",
 ["Samāna, which digests experience into understanding: give time and quiet, and do not pile on more.","Prāṇa, which takes in: the pupil needs still more input, since he has not yet had enough of it.","Udāna, which reaches upward: the pupil needs to be pushed harder, since he is not making effort.","Apāna, which lets go: the pupil must forget the lesson, since it is only weighing on his mind."],0,
 "In the body samāna is digestion; in the mind it is the same movement, turning an experience into understanding. Weak, and experience sits there raw and undigested. As with food, the cure is not more but time and quiet to digest what is already there.",
 "Samāna digests experience; give it time","Part 2"),
judge("“A panicking person can be calmed by telling them firmly to calm down, because the mind answers to a direct order.”",F,
 "The mind is the top of the keyboard, too quick to grab directly, and telling someone to calm down often makes it worse. The breath is lower and slower and answers to intention, so you take hold of that and the mind follows it down.",
 "You cannot order the mind to calm","Part 3"),
mc("U","Why does slowing the breath settle the mind, in Swamiji’s picture of the boat and the swell?",
 ["The breath is a slow, strong wave and the quick mind falls into step with it, as a small boat with a long swell.","The breath sends oxygen to the brain, which is the only reason a slow breath should have any effect.","The breath distracts the mind, so it forgets what was troubling it for as long as the breath is slow.","The breath is a habit of the lungs, and a mind that has a habit of its own can be set free of it."],0,
 "At about six breaths a minute, longer out than in, the heart and breath synchronise, heart-rate variability becomes healthily flexible, and the rest-and-restore branch switches on. One act lays down a slow reference, lowers the noise, steadies the gain and settles the mind’s own pace.",
 "The breath is the slow swell the mind rides","Part 3"),
mc("A","A teenager has gone flat and distant, and Sarah would have called it sulking. How does Swamiji read it?",
 ["As protection: a nervous system that has turned the volume down, so help it feel safe enough to come back up.","As defiance, which is to be met with firmness, so that the teenager learns it will not be allowed.","As laziness, which is to be met with a stricter timetable, so that no free time is left to waste.","As a passing mood, which is to be left alone, since any attempt to help will only make it worse."],0,
 "The shutdown state is tamas: numbness, heaviness, disconnection. It is not weakness; the system is still alive, still experiencing, but heavily and faintly. Meeting it as protection rather than defiance changes everything you do next.",
 "Shutdown is protection, not defiance","Part 4"),
judge("“Sattva is nothing more than a state of the nervous system, and the body’s settled state is all that the word means.”",F,
 "The three states of the vagus nerve map closely onto the guṇas, and slow breath is a real door to the settled state. But the deepest meaning of sattva reaches far beyond the nervous system. This layer is real, one of the layers the tradition was pointing at, and a door you can open today.",
 "Sattva reaches beyond the nervous system","Part 4"),
mc("A","A survivor feels terror at nothing more than a tone of voice, and talking alone has not helped. What does the lesson suggest?",
 ["Work with the body as well: gentle movement, releasing held tension, and slow, deep breath soften the pattern.","Talk about it more often and for longer, since the fear is held in the thoughts and the thoughts can be changed.","Avoid every tone of voice that is like it, since the pattern will fade once it has no chance to start.","Accept it as a fixed trait, since a fear that is held in the body cannot be changed by anything."],0,
 "Past conditioning is stored in the muscles as well as in memory: tightness, a held breath, a braced posture long after the danger is gone. You cannot reason someone out of a fear held in the muscles and the breath. This is why body-based therapies reach what talking cannot.",
 "Conditioning is in the body, so work with it","Part 5"),
mc("A","Kai is asked to take a baseline of his thoughts, slow his breath for five minutes, and then notice again. What is this for?",
 ["To make a test of his own: let the change in the pace of his thoughts be his evidence that body moves mind.","To prove to Swamiji that the teaching is right, so that Kai can report the result at the next meeting.","To empty his mind completely, so that after five minutes no thought is left to notice at all.","To find out how many breaths he can take in a minute, so as to compare with the others in the group."],0,
 "Kai is the sceptic; the practice is testable. Four counts in, six out. The aim is not silence or a score but his own evidence, not Swamiji’s say-so.",
 "Run the experiment and let it be your evidence","Practical situation")])
